{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Let childcare & education settings keep adrenaline for children with allergies",
        "additional_details": "It is unfair that access to emergency allergy medication depends on where a child is. Schools can buy spare adrenaline devices, but many nurseries, childminders, colleges, clubs and youth groups cannot. Families worry; staff may have to respond without spare medication. We ask the Government to amend MHRA regulations so non-school education, childcare and youth settings can choose to buy and hold spare adrenaline devices, including auto-injectors, nasal sprays and future approved devices.",
        "background": "Amend the regulations so non-school childcare and education settings\u2014including nurseries, childminders, after-school and holiday clubs, and post16 colleges\u2014can buy and keep spare adrenaline devices, with suitable safeguards and training.",
